Package: hyperspectR
Title: Hyperspectral Imaging Analysis for Biomedical Applications
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("R.", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
        role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742")),
    person("V.", "Forstmeier", role = "aut"))
Description: Reads, processes, analyzes and visualizes hyperspectral imaging
    (HSI) data from Cubert snapshot cameras, Diaspective Vision 'TIVITA'
    recordings and standard 'ENVI' and 'TIFF' files. Provides calibration
    workflows (dark correction, white reference normalization), spectral
    preprocessing (Savitzky-Golay smoothing, standard normal variate (SNV),
    multiplicative scatter correction (MSC), derivatives), dimensionless
    spectral indices, research hemoglobin fraction fitting, dimensionality
    reduction (principal component analysis (PCA), minimum noise fraction
    (MNF)), pixel classification (spectral angle mapper (SAM), support vector
    machines (SVM), random forest) and constrained spectral unmixing. Includes
    an interactive 'shiny' explorer, reproducible batch recipes and grouped
    evaluation tools. Results are research outputs; clinical or
    device-specific accuracy is not established by the included synthetic
    examples.
